NAME='Venus'
COVER_SUB='How you love and what you value in each sign.'
T=[
('Detriment','Venus in Aries, in Mars’s house, is in detriment: pronounced sensuality, relationships lived with ardour, but a certain inconstancy and a risk of sentimental disappointments. Enthusiasm at the start can fade, and rash decisions multiply when Mars is strained. Jyotish rates Mars neutral toward Venus. You like the chase and say what you want. Karmic reading: a heart learning to commit after the conquest. The lesson: closeness grows after the first fire.'),
('Own sign','Venus is at home in Taurus: it gives psychophysical balance, good humour, charm and a strong sensitivity to everything beautiful, concrete or abstract. Feelings are stable, with a gift for art, luxury goods and beauty care; finances and romantic success are favoured. Jyotish gives Venus own-sign strength here. Under strain: excess sensuality, jealousy and obstinacy. Karmic reading: a heart learning self-worth without possession. The shadow is possessiveness. The lesson: love is a garden, not a possession.'),
('Playful','Venus in Gemini joins Venus’s amiability and charm to Mercury’s subtle perception and gives a special engaging sympathy, with poetic and literary gifts and a talent for manual arts. Friendships are many more than deep, and short trips bring new friends. Jyotish counts Mercury as a friend of Venus. Karmic reading: a heart learning to move from many contacts to one real bond. The shadow is lightness that avoids depth. The lesson: staying interested in one person is its own adventure.'),
('Tender','Venus in Cancer, when harmonious, shows great love of family, versatility, sweetness, diplomacy and personal magnetism, especially favourable in feminine themes. Taste and creative imagination suit careers in interior design and fashion. Jyotish counts the Moon as an enemy of Venus, so affection and pleasure sometimes pull apart. Karmic reading: a heart carrying old protections and fears of abandonment. The shadow is clinging and moodiness. The lesson: say what you need instead of waiting to be guessed.'),
('Generous','Venus in Leo favours emotional life, with strong physical and sensual vitality, a tendency to idealise the beloved and a love of children, with an artistic sense and a taste for luxury, splendour and spectacle. Jyotish counts the Sun as an enemy of Venus, so the heart wants admiration more than ease. Bonds can bring economic advantage. Under strain: possessive love. Karmic reading: a heart learning to give without needing applause. The shadow is vanity. The lesson: real love can be quiet.'),
('Fall','Venus is in its fall in Virgo, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here, deepest at 27°. Affection leans toward rationality over sentiment, with good taste, manual skill, artistic aptitude and a talent for therapies that restore body and mind. You notice flaws and can be shy, critical and hard on yourself. Mercury, a friend of Venus in Jyotish, helps with practical love. Karmic reading: a heart purifying through service. The lesson: love does not have to be earned flawlessly.'),
('Own sign','Venus is at home in Libra, its night house, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength. It brings great sensitivity, noble feeling, moral rectitude and a deep sense of justice, with a strong sense of aesthetics. Its signature is the need to please others and to find healthy pleasure and love as the finest feeling of the soul. Karmic reading: a heart learning relationship as balance. The shadow is avoiding conflict. The lesson: choose a partner out of freedom, not fear of being alone.'),
('Detriment','Venus in Scorpio, in Mars’s house, is in detriment: it cannot express its balance of feeling. The nature is strongly sensual and eroticism so rooted it can turn deaf to argument, sometimes becoming an obsession. Jyotish rates Mars neutral toward Venus. You want depth, truth and total commitment. Karmic reading: a heart passing through jealousy, loss and renewal. The shadow is possessiveness and testing. The lesson: intimacy needs trust, not surveillance.'),
('Free','Venus in Sagittarius, in Jupiter’s house, gives amiability and sympathy, a bent for philosophy and literature, spiritual elevation and a love of healthy pleasures, travel, art and history. Contact with foreigners is favoured and sometimes profitable. Jyotish rates Jupiter neutral toward Venus. Under strain: showing off, dogmatism. Karmic reading: a heart seeking meaning in love. The shadow is restlessness and promising more than you can give. The lesson: a good partner is also a good travelling companion.'),
('Loyal','Venus in sober, cool Capricorn has its sweetness, affection and expansiveness neutralised, and reason takes over from sentiment, yet feelings are firm and faithful, especially with Saturn and Jupiter. Career and social position are often helped by women. Jyotish counts Saturn as a friend of Venus. Karmic reading: a heart that learned to guard itself and now learns to trust. The shadow is coldness and treating relationships as projects. The lesson: warmth is not a luxury.'),
('Friendly','Venus in electric Aquarius draws a personality to original and avant-garde ideas of art, with creativity and a taste for scientific novelty. You are more cerebral than sentimental, and affection is enriched by shared interests. Jyotish counts Saturn as a friend of Venus. Strained with Uranus or Saturn: risk of separation. Karmic reading: a heart learning friendship as the base of love. The shadow is detachment and fear of being tied down. The lesson: a close bond can still leave you free.'),
('Exalted','Venus is exalted in Pisces, and Jyotish agrees, placing its peak at 27°. It brings deep inner richness and a strong emotional charge, usually two important situations in life. You guard your feelings, often hide them and may live platonic loves intensely. Sensitivity, understanding, devotion, generosity and indulgence toward others increase. Karmic reading: a heart that loves unconditionally and must learn boundaries. The shadow is idealising and self-sacrifice. The lesson: you can love without losing yourself.'),
]
